This is the bootloader
It is UEFI, NOT Legacy BIOS compatible

efi.h - header for uefi return flags, services, protocols, etc.
    I mainly used AI to write headers and I checked if it is okay
    using the official documentation at https://uefi.org/
    Not all featurs are supported I am trying to make it simple
    before supporting C/Cpp. It's content is flaged by comments for what is what used.
    (example --- boot services --- flags headers and services needed for boot services)
uefi.c - Main boot file, the first thing that reaches the uefi, there are 2 versions
        1. uefi.c.new - a remake of uefi.c (deciding about refactoring uefi.c)
        2. uefi.c - is what I have described earlier, mainly collects information
           loads kernel and passes information to it using kernelentry kernelbuffers
           initializes GOP and passes the handler to kernel.